  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 trains `SingleDrugElasticNet` once per drug on `scale_gene_expression` features whose `StandardScaler` is fitted on the training samples of that drug; v2 fits `scaledGeneExpression` once over all training pairs and routes by drug. The two agree (class forward) when every drug has the same training samples (`shared_enet`), and differ when the drugs were measured on different samples (`ragged_enet`). This is the intended 'globally fitted single-drug featurizers' deviation of the plan (4.4).",
    "1.6.1 builds `ElasticNet(alpha, l1_ratio)` with sklearn's solver defaults and `random_state` unset; l1_ratio 0 or 1 select Ridge or Lasso. The v2 predictor pins the same solver settings (max_iter=1000, tol=1e-4, cyclic, random_state=None; `non_tunable_hyperparameters`), so the effective parameters, including `random_state`, are equal and the per-drug coefficients agree to float32 precision without any override.",
    "Defaults agree: 1.6.1 first grid point is l1_ratio=0.2, alpha=1 (grids l1_ratio 0.2/0.5/0.9, alpha 1/0.8/0.6/0.4/0.1/0.01/5); the v2 defaults are l1_ratio=0.2, alpha=1.0. The `defaults` variant runs the unmodified preset.",
    "1.6.1 selects `landmark_genes` while loading; the v2 preset selects the same list with `scaledGeneExpression(gene_list=landmark_genes)`. The synthetic gene names are in no shipped list, so both sides get a pre-selected matrix and the selection itself is not compared here.",
    "v2 features are float32; the `identical` steps feed both estimators the same float64 matrix and are exact."
  ],
